# SQL's `IS NOT NULL` after a parenthesized operand, inside `and`: the fix drops the extra parentheses.
mode: syntax
---- query
from 'orders.csv' | where (amount + 1) IS NOT NULL and amount > 2
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..66
  PIPELINE@0..65
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    LITERAL@5..17
      STRING@5..17 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@17..18 " "
    PIPE@18..19 "|"
    WHITESPACE@19..20 " "
    WHERE_OP@20..65
      IDENT@20..25 "where"
      WHITESPACE@25..26 " "
      BIN_EXPR@26..65
        BIN_EXPR@26..50
          PAREN_EXPR@26..38
            L_PAREN@26..27 "("
            BIN_EXPR@27..37
              NAME_REF@27..33
                IDENT@27..33 "amount"
              WHITESPACE@33..34 " "
              PLUS@34..35 "+"
              WHITESPACE@35..36 " "
              LITERAL@36..37
                LONG@36..37 "1"
            R_PAREN@37..38 ")"
          WHITESPACE@38..39 " "
          IDENT@39..41 "IS"
          WHITESPACE@41..42 " "
          IDENT@42..45 "NOT"
          WHITESPACE@45..46 " "
          IDENT@46..50 "NULL"
        WHITESPACE@50..51 " "
        AND_KW@51..54 "and"
        WHITESPACE@54..55 " "
        BIN_EXPR@55..65
          NAME_REF@55..61
            IDENT@55..61 "amount"
          WHITESPACE@61..62 " "
          GT@62..63 ">"
          WHITESPACE@63..64 " "
          LITERAL@64..65
            LONG@64..65 "2"
  WHITESPACE@65..66 "\n"

error[DS0105]: `IS NOT NULL` is SQL, not DataScript
  --> query:1:40
  |
1 | from 'orders.csv' | where (amount + 1) IS NOT NULL and amount > 2
  |                                        ^^^^^^^^^^^ this is SQL's null test
  |
  = help: test for null with `isnotnull(...)`: `isnotnull(amount + 1)`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    from 'orders.csv' | where isnotnull(amount + 1) and amount > 2
which parses without errors
